3.12 Deliberately not covered in STA530
The slides list what the session leaves out:

maximum-likelihood derivations;
instrumental variables / generalized method of moments (GMM) estimation;
higher-order spatial models;
spatial Durbin and SLX models (which add WX, the neighbours’ covariates);
geographically weighted regression (GWR) and other spatial heterogeneity models.

The stated goal: understand what spatial dependence means, recognize basic models, and interpret them responsibly — not become spatial econometricians in 90 minutes.
